INSERT INTO public.super_admin_docs (slug, title, category, summary, content_md, tags, is_pinned, sort_order) VALUES
(
  'docs-readme',
  'How the Docs Tab Works',
  'meta',
  'A short guide to creating, editing and linking internal admin documentation.',
  E'# How the Docs Tab Works\n\nThis tab is your **internal explainer / whitepaper library** — only visible to super admins.\n\n## What goes here\n- Architecture overviews (Mesh, Oracle, Bubble Map, etc.)\n- System walkthroughs you ask the AI to generate\n- Decision logs and "how does X actually work?" explainers\n- Anything you want to reference later without re-asking\n\n## How to add a doc\n1. Click **+ New Doc** in the top right of this tab.\n2. Give it a **title** (becomes the heading) and a **slug** (URL-safe id like `mesh-overview`).\n3. Pick a **category** (e.g. `architecture`, `oracle`, `mesh`, `meta`, `general`).\n4. Write the body in **Markdown**. Internal links work — for example:\n   - [Open the Oracle tab](/super-admin?tab=oracle)\n   - [Mesh Viewer](/super-admin?tab=oracle&sub=mesh-viewer)\n   - [Insiders Lifecycle](/super-admin?tab=insiders-lifecycle)\n5. Hit **Save**. You can edit or delete any time.\n\n## How the AI uses this\nWhen you ask "give me the overview of X again", the AI can write the explainer **straight into a new doc entry** instead of dumping it in chat. You then refer back here whenever you want — no scrolling.\n\n## Markdown cheatsheet\n- `# Heading` → big heading\n- `**bold**` → **bold**\n- `` `code` `` → inline code\n- `- item` → bullet list\n- `[label](/path)` → internal link\n- `[label](https://example.com)` → external link\n\n## Pinning\nToggle **Pinned** on important docs and they bubble to the top of the list.',
  ARRAY['meta','guide'],
  true,
  0
),
(
  'mesh-and-oracle-overview',
  'Mesh + Oracle Ecosystem Overview',
  'architecture',
  'How tokens and developers enter the Reputation Mesh, how they get rated, and a map of all 13 Oracle sub-tabs.',
  E'# Mesh + Oracle Ecosystem Overview\n\n_Last refreshed from the audit walkthrough._\n\n## 1. Data Funnel — How things enter the Mesh\n\nTokens and devs arrive via several **ingest points** and get enriched before they land in `reputation_mesh` (~424k links currently).\n\n**Ingest sources:**\n- **Pump.fun stream** — every new mint detected by the pumpfun monitor\n- **𝕏 / Twitter** — handles harvested by the social mesh linker\n- **Helius webhooks** — wallet activity → triggers family discovery\n- **Manual lookups** — anything you search in [Intel Lookup](/super-admin?tab=oracle&sub=intel-lookup)\n\n**Enrichment functions:**\n- `oracle-master-spider` — multi-source crawler\n- `family-discovery-engine` — clusters wallets into families\n- `social-mesh-linker` — links tokens ↔ socials ↔ devs\n- `universal-mesh-feeder` — the catch-all indexer\n\n## 2. Rating & Trust System\n\n### `developer_profiles.trust_level`\n| Level | Trigger |\n|---|---|\n| `trusted` | integrity score ≥ 70 |\n| `neutral` | default |\n| `suspicious` | mixed signals |\n| `scammer` | rugs ≥ 2 |\n\n### Automation\n- **Hourly cron** → auto-promotes `scammer` devs into [pumpfun_blacklist](/super-admin?tab=oracle&sub=blacklist-mesh)\n- **30-min cron** → auto-promotes `trusted` devs into [pumpfun_whitelist](/super-admin?tab=oracle&sub=whitelist-mesh)\n- Blacklist has grown **54 → 152** since launch\n\n### `reputation_mesh.confidence`\nA 0–100 score on each *link* (not the entity). Quantifies "how sure are we this dev owns this wallet / posted this tweet / minted this token."\n\n## 3. The 13 Oracle Sub-Tabs\n\nAll under [Super Admin → Oracle](/super-admin?tab=oracle):\n\n| # | Sub-tab | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 🕸️ Mesh Pipeline | Live stats + manual triggers for spider/feeder jobs |\n| 2 | 🗺️ Mesh Viewer | Tabular view of all mesh links, with the ✏️ Verdict Editor |\n| 3 | 🚫 Blacklist Mesh | Auto + manually promoted scammer devs |\n| 4 | ✅ Whitelist Mesh | Trusted devs cleared for trading guards |\n| 5 | 🔗 Team Intel | Wallet-family clustering output |\n| 6 | 🔍 Intel Lookup | Free-form search for any wallet / token / @handle |\n| 7 | 👥 Developer Profiles | All known devs + their trust level |\n| 8 | 🚨 Developer Alerts | New mint alerts from tracked devs |\n| 9 | ⭐ Allstar Registry | Top-tier proven devs (ATH ≥ $100k) |\n| 10 | 🧬 Genealogy | Funding chain tracer (Mint → Funder → KYC Root) |\n| 11 | 🪪 Manual KYC | Human override panel for KYC roots |\n| 12 | 📊 Insiders Lifecycle | Per-token entry → peak journey + Promote/Reject buttons |\n| 13 | 🛠️ Health & Toggles | Feature flags + system health checks |\n\n> Direct deep-link example: [Mesh Viewer](/super-admin?tab=oracle&sub=mesh-viewer)\n\n## 4. Manual Curation\n\nTwo recently-added override surfaces:\n\n### A. [Insiders Lifecycle](/super-admin?tab=insiders-lifecycle) → Per-row Actions\n- **Promote** → push the dev into the trusted whitelist\n- **Reject** → flag as scammer, push into blacklist\n- **Reconsider** → reset to neutral, re-queue for re-evaluation\n\n### B. Mesh Verdict Editor (pencil icon in [Mesh Viewer](/super-admin?tab=oracle&sub=mesh-viewer))\n- Adjust `confidence` 0–100\n- Override `relationship_type`\n- Add a manual `notes` field that overrides automated reasoning\n\n## 5. Status & Gaps\n\n### ✅ Working well\n- Automated blacklist growth (54 → 152)\n- Healthy mesh intake: 2k–10k links/day\n- Manual override loop is closed (UI → DB → guards)\n\n### ⚠️ Known gaps\n- **Overlap** between `dev_wallet_reputation` and `developer_profiles` — needs reconciliation\n- `token_fingerprints` table is **empty** — fingerprinting job not running\n- `co_mint_clusters` table is **empty** — co-mint detector not wired up\n\n## 6. Quick links\n- [Oracle tab root](/super-admin?tab=oracle)\n- [Insiders Lifecycle](/super-admin?tab=insiders-lifecycle)\n- [Allstars](/super-admin?tab=allstar)\n- [Pump.fun monitor](/super-admin?tab=pumpfun-monitor)',
  ARRAY['mesh','oracle','architecture','overview'],
  true,
  1
)
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;